title: markowitz-optimizer
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hekimoglu
    given-names: Fatih
    email: fatih.hekim1@hotmail.com
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch, research-grade Python toolkit for mean-variance portfolio
  optimization. Implements the closed-form efficient frontier, numerical
  optimizer with linear and box constraints, Ledoit-Wolf and Oracle
  Approximating Shrinkage covariance estimators, the Black-Litterman posterior
  in Theil mixed-estimation form, the Idzorek (2005) confidence mapping, and a
  walk-forward backtest engine with proportional transaction costs. Validated
  against PyPortfolioOpt, scikit-learn, and the He-Litterman (1999) tabulated
  results.
keywords:
  - portfolio-optimization
  - quantitative-finance
  - mean-variance
  - black-litterman
  - ledoit-wolf
